<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  NFM-5112 D1-tighten — Burst-window MLX runner max-lifetime watchdog
  (cadence tightened from 25 min → 22 min per CTO escalation NFM-5079).

  Why this plist exists (separate label from NFM-5080's):
    3 wedges on 09-21 slipped through the 25 min cadence (wedges arrived
    at cycle minute 26-30). Tightening to 22 min closes the wedge-formation
    gap (now <20 min) below the observed 30 min no-progress window.

  Why a NEW plist (not an edit to NFM-5080's):
    - Charter hygiene: additive invocation surface, no source modification
      to the chokepoint (sha 37a69e1f0fb6 preserved), no probe changes
      to lightrag-watchdog, no changes to the reingest 03:30Z trigger.
    - Rollback symmetry: any of the two plists can be independently
      disabled without disturbing the other. CR/RE can A/B the two
      cadences without overwriting each other's running config.
    - AC2 (CR verification) wants an isolated, byte-diffable surface so
      schedule arithmetic can be inspected independently of the existing
      plist's evidence trail.

  Schedule (UTC + local +08:00 — 22 min spacing, ±60s tolerance):
    03:30Z  →  11:30 local   (first post-03:30Z reingest fire)
    03:52Z  →  11:52 local   (+22m)
    04:14Z  →  12:14 local   (+44m)
    04:36Z  →  12:36 local   (+66m)
    04:58Z  →  12:58 local   (+88m)
    05:20Z  →  13:20 local   (+110m, last, on the burst-window boundary)

  Spacing verification (CR AC2):
    03:30→03:52 = 22 min, 03:52→04:14 = 22 min, 04:14→04:36 = 22 min,
    04:36→04:58 = 22 min, 04:58→05:20 = 22 min. 6 fires total.
    Off-burst: NO firings (soak behavior unchanged from NFM-5080).

  Identity: runs in the lwj04 user-session launchd domain (gui/$UID).
  The MLX runner is owned by lwj04 (same desktop user), so the chokepoint's
  existing sudoers grant (for nfmdeploy → root) is NOT consumed — lwj04
  can SIGTERM own processes directly. No sudoers change. Chokepoint
  byte-identical before/after deploy (sha 37a69e1f0fb6).

  Hard constraints honored:
    - chokepoint sha 37a69e1f0fb6 preserved (NFM-4922 RCA, NFM-5080 charter)
    - auto-unwedge path unchanged (NFM-4887)
    - no probe changes to lightrag-watchdog
    - no changes to reingest 03:30Z trigger
    - new invocation surface only (plist + schedule modification)
    - sibling NFM-5080 plist (local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime) left UNTOUCHED

  Wrapper script is the SAME as NFM-5080's:
    /Users/lwj04/.local/nfm/runner-maxlifetime.sh
  Only the invocation cadence changes; the chokepoint call site is
  identical. No wrapper script modification required.

  Convention (matches ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime.plist):
    - NO RunAtLoad: install does NOT fire immediately
    - NO KeepAlive: each fire is independent
    - Label prefix local.nfm.* per charter hygiene
    - Label distinct from NFM-5080's so launchctl can disambiguate

  Rollback (AC3, 2 commands):
    launchctl bootout gui/$UID/local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime-tightened
    launchctl bootout gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime-tightened.plist
  (first form targets the LaunchAgent label; second form targets the
  deployed plist by its absolute path under ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ —
  a bare filename resolves under ~ and the bootout silently fails.)

  Deploy (RE):
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID \
      ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime-tightened.plist

  Verify (RE):
    launchctl list | grep runner-maxlifetime-tightened
    plutil -p ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime-tightened.plist

  Acceptance evidence (NFM-5111 AC):
    - Schedule arithmetic: plutil -p on deployed plist (CR-side AC2)
    - Chokepoint sha unchanged: shasum -a 256 /usr/local/lib/nfm-g2/ollama-runner-term.sh
    - Loaded status: launchctl list | grep runner-maxlifetime-tightened
    - Burst-window restart count (after deploy):
        grep -c "D1 fire:" ~/.local/nfm/runner-maxlifetime.log
        (wrapper's primary log /var/log/nfm-g2/runner-maxlifetime.log is
        not writable on this host; the wrapper falls back to the above path)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>local.nfm.runner-maxlifetime-tightened</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/lwj04/.local/nfm/runner-maxlifetime.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key><integer>11</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key><integer>11</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>52</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key><integer>12</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>14</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key><integer>12</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>36</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key><integer>12</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>58</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Hour</key><integer>13</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer>
        </dict>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/lwj04/.local/nfm/runner-maxlifetime-tightened-launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/lwj04/.local/nfm/runner-maxlifetime-tightened-launchd.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>